# EVERY FUSION THAT OWES ITS PARTS AN EQUALITY, AND WHETHER THE SUM IS OWED AT ALL. One row per
# composed layer reached by at least one part.
#
# ⛔⛔⛔ THE UNITS ARE NOT CHECKED HERE AND MUST NOT BE. conformance/README.md:326 -- "the units
#    of a fusion's parts are NOT checked and must not be ... asserting that they name one unit
#    IS WHAT A FUSION SAYS." A filer who fuses two layers has DECLARED them commensurable, and
#    a checker that tested it would be overruling a judgement no document owes it. This is the
#    one site on the roster whose empty guard is correct, which is why `(forbidden)` is a value
#    and not a NULL.
#
# ⭐⭐ SUSPENDED IS A THIRD OUTCOME BESIDE PASSED AND FAILED. A composer who never searched for
#    double counting, or who found it and could not size it, owes no equality -- so the rows
#    composition/suspended_fusions.sqlc names are absent from the arithmetic rather than
#    passing it. assertion.xsd:1934 states the verdict table this follows.
#
# ⛔ THE VERDICT COMES FROM composition/owed_equality.sqlc AND THE REASON FROM ITS COMPLEMENT.
#   This file used to re-derive the anti-join while its own `--` line cited the relation that
#   already held it -- a header documenting the dependency it declined to compose. Taking the
#   verdict from the named relation is what makes a change to `owed_equality` reach here.
# ⚠️ THE REASON JOIN IS NARROWED TO THE DEMAND GRAIN, AND IT HAS TO BE. This site computes the
#   demand sum, and composition/suspension_grounds.sqlc is one row per (composed layer, ground)
#   carrying the quantity it lifts -- a BAG. composition/suspended_fusions.sqlc is its
#   projection onto the fusion, and this site needs the reasons, so it folds the bag itself. Without the narrowing a nameplate-only suspension
#   would supply this site's reason, and TWO grounds on one fusion would emit two rows for one
#   candidate -- which algebra/arithmetic_class.sqlc would catch as a partition failure, but the
#   cause would be this join rather than anything a document filed.
#   ⭐ At most one ground can apply per quantity because assertion.xsd makes StatedEliminations
#   an xs:choice: a fusion files an `absent` or `elimination+`, never both. That is a grammar
#   guarantee the DDL does not carry, which is why the narrowing is written rather than assumed.
-- asrt:Fusion/asrt:Part against asrt:Eliminations, via composition/owed_equality.sqlc.
SELECT a.site, p.filing, p.layer, p.verdict, p.detail
FROM      (
    :compose(arithmetic/roster.sqlc)
) a
LEFT JOIN (
    SELECT f.filing, f.layer,
           CASE WHEN o.filing IS NULL THEN 'suspended'
                ELSE 'computable' END AS verdict,
           CASE WHEN o.filing IS NULL
                     THEN format('no equality is owed: %s', s.suspended_because)
                ELSE 'the sum is owed exactly' END AS detail
    FROM      (
        :compose(composition/fusions.sqlc)
    ) f
    LEFT JOIN (
        :compose(composition/owed_equality.sqlc)
    ) o USING (filing, layer)
    -- ⛔ THE GROUNDS ARE A BAG, so they are folded to one row per fusion before the join.
    --   Joining the bag directly turned fourteen fusions into seventeen rows the day a third
    --   ground was added; `composition/suspended_fusions.sqlc` is the set, and this needs the
    --   REASONS as well, so it aggregates them rather than reaching for the projection.
    LEFT JOIN (
        SELECT g.composition, g.composed_layer,
               string_agg(DISTINCT g.suspended_because, '; ' ORDER BY g.suspended_because)
                   AS suspended_because
        FROM (
            :compose(composition/suspension_grounds.sqlc)
        ) g
        WHERE coalesce(g.quantity, 'demand') = 'demand'
        GROUP BY g.composition, g.composed_layer
    ) s ON s.composition = f.filing AND s.composed_layer = f.layer
) p ON true
WHERE a.slug = 'fusion_sum'
